! <solver:p610_t3>
! Heathrow Express Trial Tunnel - three-stage NATM benchmark (Mohr-Coulomb, T3 plane strain).
! 
!   Geometry  : half-symmetric vertical section through tunnel axis (x = 0 is symmetry).
!               Tunnel radius a = 4.25 m  |  axis depth z0 = 20 m  |  crown at y = +4.25 m.
!               Model width  x in [0, 25] m   (~6 a, far-field).
!               Model height y in [-15, +20] m (ground surface at y = +20 m).
! 
!   Soil      : London Clay, drained-equivalent Mohr-Coulomb (operational stiffness).
!               phi'=22.5 deg, c'=50 kPa, psi=0 deg, gamma=19.5 kN/m^3, E=100 MPa, nu=0.30, K0=1.0.
!               Cohesion and stiffness sized so a drained MC model with K0=1.0 reproduces
!               the operational shear response of short-term London Clay around the cavity;
!               see Help.md for the rationale.
! 
!   Excavation sequence (3 stages):
!       Stage 1 - TOP HEADING:  upper half of disc (y > 0)               -> 10 T3 elements
!       Stage 2 - BENCH:        middle band (-4.25/2 <= y <= 0)             ->  6 T3 elements
!       Stage 3 - INVERT:       lower band (y < -4.25/2)                    ->  4 T3 elements
!       Total excavated = 20 of 126 T3 elements (10 cells x 2).
! 
!   Mesh      : graded rectangular T3 mesh, conforming to tunnel radius at i=3 (x=4.25 m)
!               and j=2/6 (y = -+4.25 m). Cell-centroid test r_c < a marks tunnel elements;
!               the resulting boundary is stair-stepped (acceptable for displacement-level
!               verification at +-15 percent vs published trough magnitudes).
! 
!   References:
!       Deane & Bassett (1995), Proc ICE Geotech Eng 113(3), 144-156.
!       Mair, Taylor & Burland (1996), Geotech Aspects of Underground Constr in Soft Ground.
!       New & Bowers (1994), Proc ICE Geotech Eng 107(2), 73-83.
! 
! <BEGIN:AnalysisOptions>
! failure_criterion MohrCoulomb
! material_type Isotropic
! mesh_type T3
! solver_executable p610_t3_mohr_coulomb
! <END:AnalysisOptions>
!
! <BEGIN:Header>
! nels  nn  np_types
126  80  1
! <END:Header>
!
! <BEGIN:Materials>
! phi(deg)  c(kPa)  psi(deg)  gamma(kN/m^3)  E(kPa)  nu(-)  K0(-)  (one value per line, per material type)
22.5
30
0
19.5
60000
0.30
1.0
! <END:Materials>
